INT. COMPETITIVE PIE-BAKING TENT, COUNTY FAIR - DAY

Rows of folding tables. Flour hangs in sunbeams like pollen. A banner reads: 87TH ANNUAL PIE CHAMPIONSHIP. A judge's gavel sits next to a bell.

Six contestants stand behind their pies in tight, silent ranks.

AGATHA "AGGIE" LINDQUIST-REYES (60s, blue ribbon pinned to apron, jaw set) polishes a lattice crust with a pastry brush. Beside her, LONNIE BIGGS (40s, sweating through a chef's coat, flour on his eyebrows) arranges cherries with tweezers. At the next station, the young prodigy MEI-LING ARROYO (16, braids, calm as a monk) lets her pie rest. Behind them, SIGMUND PRATT (70s, bolo tie, hands tremble) hums a hymn. At the end of the row, twin sisters DOROTHEA and DELPHINE VASQUEZ-MOORE (50s, identical aprons, identical glares) tap the same rhythm on their tables.

A JUDGE in a straw boater strolls the line, clipboard in hand. He stops at Aggie.

JUDGE
Mrs. Lindquist-Reyes. Third time in the final. Nervous?

AGGIE
Never.

Her brush twitches. Lonnie watches it twitch.

JUDGE
(to Lonnie)
And you, young man?

LONNIE
Oh, I'm great. Great! Totally relaxed!

A cherry rolls off his tweezers and across the table. He does not move. Everyone watches it roll. It stops against Mei-Ling's pie. She regards it, then flicks it back to him with one finger.

The judge raises his bell.

DOROTHEA
^Don't you dare.

DELPHINE
^Don't you dare.

The twins speak as one, to each other. Neither blinks. The judge rings the bell.

All six lift their forks like swords. The tent goes still. Sigmund's hymn gets louder, then stops mid-note.

The judge cuts into Aggie's pie. Steam rises. He takes a bite. Chews. His face reveals nothing.

JUDGE
Hm.

Aggie's brush finally falls from her hand.
